॰ ॥ कार्यक्रमपठनम् ॥
॰ प्रवेशद्वारम् ऽ सर्वाः घोषणाः पठति ऽ घोषणासङ्ख्यां ददाति ।

सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः कार्यक्रमपठनम् आदाय दैर्घ्य ॱॱ न६४ ददाति दोषयुक्त न६४ आदि
    ॰ ONE-BASED, W-164. This read from ० and the first token is at १.
    ॰
    ॰ `पदविभाग` resets `चिह्नकसूचकाङ्क` to ० and every `चिह्नकयोजनम्`
    ॰ ADVANCES BEFORE WRITING — the appender idiom every arena in this corpus
    ॰ uses — so tokens occupy १..N and slot ० is never written, holding the
    ॰ reserved `शून्यम्`. Reading from ० took that शून्यम् and raised
    ॰ "`ॱ भेद` read from Nil"; the loop also stopped one token SHORT at the far
    ॰ end. The T1 parser could not read the T1 lexer's output at all.
    ॰
    ॰ NOTHING CAUGHT IT BECAUSE NOTHING RAN THE PAIR: the lexer and the parser
    ॰ are tested separately, and every parser test builds its input by calling
    ॰ the appenders directly rather than by lexing source. Both halves passed
    ॰ while the seam was broken. The end-to-end test in t1_execution.rs is what
    ॰ found it, and exists so the pair cannot come apart again silently.
    ॰
    ॰ THE PARSER IS THE SIDE THAT MOVED, and deliberately: the lexer follows the
    ॰ corpus-wide idiom, so it is the reader that was out of step. W-163 records
    ॰ the same class of mismatch one layer up, in the opposite direction — the
    ॰ real defect is that the convention is nowhere stated normatively.
    पठनस्थान भवति १ ।
    ॰ ॥ AND THE MATCH CACHE IS EMPTIED HERE ॥ Position 5 is a DIFFERENT token in
    ॰ the next program, so a cache that survives between programs makes the second
    ॰ one read the first one's text. That is the same class as the empty-literal
    ॰ defect this corpus just paid for — a value that outlives the program it was
    ॰ taken from, passing only because of what ran before it.
    मेलनस्थानम् भवति ० ।
    चिह्नकदैर्घ्य भवति आरभ्य दैर्घ्य योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
    घोषणासूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    दोषसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    मण्डलनामसूचकाङ्क भवति ० ।
    उपेक्षितचिह्नकसंख्या भवति ० ।

    ॰ W-230 (2026-09-04): THIS LOOP'S STEP IS INSIDE ITS CALLS. The condition
    ॰ reads `पठनस्थान` and no statement of the body assigns it: every arm
    ॰ advances the cursor through `मेलनम्` (the keyword test, which consumes
    ॰ on a match) or `अग्रिमम्` (the skip, which reads and advances), directly
    ॰ or inside `वृत्तिपठनम्`/`संरचनापठनम्`/`गणनापठनम्`/`मण्डलचरपठनम्`. Of the
    ॰ corpus's 237 loops it is the one that steps neither in its own body nor
    ॰ by return (W-207), and the loop census now follows ONE CALL LEVEL —
    ॰ `मेलनम्` and `अग्रिमम्` both assign `पठनस्थान` in their own bodies — so
    ॰ the step is seen where it is. In the paradigm the step is the न letter
    ॰ inside the loop's run; here the run is the parser's, and the letter sits
    ॰ one call deep.
